      "facts": [
        "Agents that don't charge credits when credits would be very small (<5), each mapped to the models its own definition runs (current and the ones released clients still ship).",
        "Making them free avoids user confusion when they connect their own Claude subscription (BYOK) but still see credit charges for non-Claude models. The model is part of the key because a run's agent id is the client's choice; the id alone would make any model free under 5 credits.",
        "Check if an agent is a free tier agent (see FREE_TIER_AGENT_MODELS). Billing also requires one of its models: see isFreeAgentModel.",
        "Check if a free tier agent running this model should be free (no credit charge) for small requests. This is separate from FREE mode - these agents get free credits only when the cost would be trivial (<5 credits).",
        "This is separate from FREE_MODE_ALLOWED_AGENTS which is for the explicit \"free\" cost mode. These agents get free credits only when the cost would be trivial (<5 credits).",
        "Check if the current cost mode is FREE mode."
      ],
